es inside captured prose. They are graded eval inputs and recorded payloads; rewriting them would alter eval semantics.\n- `docs/adr/0055…md` cites `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/…_heldout.py`, a path stale in two ways. ADRs are historical records and `_HISTORY_PREFIXES` exempts `docs/adr/`.\n\nThe full 76-row before/after table is retained as session evidence (`b721-collect-table.md`); it is omitted here only for length."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793524811732290016,"uuid":"a84ece05-9ee4-4ac9-a67c-63de4061293b"}